[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   step_065: Operational time-equivalent of the transit rotation.
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   Every Phase-3 step expresses the comet anomaly in angular units: the
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   orig->fut periapsis-direction rotation d_of and its residual after the
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   measured encounter budget is regressed out (step_063).  Under the
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   domain-boundary reading that residual is a phase error -- a proper-time
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   offset accumulated during the boundary crossing that a standard-clock
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   reconstruction mis-assigns as an in-plane rotation.  This step converts
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   the measured rotation into an operational time-equivalent; it is not a
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   derived proper-time measurement until a field/clock response model is
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   specified.
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   Definition
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   At the 250 AU barycentric reference sphere a periapsis-direction
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   rotation d_th (radians) corresponds to the comet's sky position having
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   been swept through the same angle.  The comet sweeps sky angle at the
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   rate Omega_b = h / r_b^2, where h = sqrt(mu q (1+e)) is the specific
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   angular momentum of the boundary orbit and r_b = 250 AU.  The operational
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   time-equivalent is therefore
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   dtau = d_th * r_b^2 / h        [yr]
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   -- the time an unperturbed comet on the same boundary orbit needs to
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   subtend the unexplained rotation.  No lapse-field amplitude is assumed.
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   Two quantities are reported per comet:
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   dtau_total   : the full orig->fut rotation expressed in years
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   dtau_unexplained : the residual of dtau after regression on the
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   measured encounter budget (energy kick, minimum
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   planetary approach, perihelion depth, inclination)
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   The fractional slip dtau/(t_back + t_fwd) expresses the offset relative
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   to the comet's measured transit duration inside the 250 AU sphere -- a
[2026-09-20 11:05:24 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 065]   dimensionless lapse contrast.
